  "id": "isolated-brain",
  "term": "isolated brain",
  "definition": "In this context, an isolated brain refers to a way of viewing mental disorders as if they arise only within the brain itself. The source contrasts this with a broader model in which mood and stress-related disorders reflect linked brain, immune, endocrine, metabolic, gut, and circadian processes.",
